issues.fix_hint:
Drain the stream via its actual EventEmitter contract rather than for-await:

  function consumeResultStream(streamPromise) {
    return streamPromise.then((stream) => new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      let rows = 0;
      stream.on('data', () => { rows++; })
            .on('end', () => resolve(rows))
            .on('error', reject);
    }));
  }

(Note ResultStream enters flowing mode as soon as a 'data' listener is added and pumps one row per microtask, so end/error must be attached in the same synchronous turn — the chained form above does that.)

Alternatively, add a real `[Symbol.asyncIterator]()` to ResultStream in js/src/result-stream.ts (backed by read()/pause()/resume() with correct backpressure and error propagation) and keep the for-await here — but that is a public-API change to the published package and needs its own tests in js/test/stream.test.mjs plus a SKILL.md update, so it is the larger option.

Either way, run `node bench/vs-oxigraph.mjs` once and confirm the block completes and prints the advisory JSON before re-requesting review — the defect would have been caught by a single execution.
